2, node3 with node1 as the writable primary\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 initialized as primary (wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders, hot_standby, replicator role created) and confirmed pg_is_in_recovery=false with two active streaming replicas post-restart. node2 and node3 built via pg_basebackup -R and confirmed pg_is_in_recovery=true both before and after their restarts, streaming continuously from node1. Data written on node1 (repl_test rows) observed identically on both standbys before and after the full restart cycle.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c16d526559e24703\",\"cmd-d0d3c7d2ae0a4bef\",\"cmd-f1717d4b54ad43a7\",\"cmd-7bca66830e0e4060\",\"cmd-4bad63cc11e9439f\",\"cmd-ca1501fa4b0a4958\",\"cmd-11ab52ca33db4a58\",\"cmd-deb0fd7adeb64019\",\"cmd-117216b4bdbc44b4\",\"cmd-5474a24148514c75\",\"cmd-b04cead12b9b4cb3\",\"cmd-450b5156b79d4fb5\",\"cmd-3fe55bcae1ab41f6\",\"cmd-aa6bc68395f74d52\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2-tls-ca\",\"requirement\":\"Carry replication traffic over TLS using a certificate authority created specifically for this cluster\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A self-signed CA (CN=pg-repl-cluster-ca) was generated on node1 (openssl genrsa + req -x509), and per-node server certs (node1/node2/node3) plus a replicator client cert were issued from that CA (openssl x509 -req -CA ca.crt -CAkey ca.key). All three nodes have ssl=on with ssl_cert_file/ssl_key_file/ssl_ca_file pointing to these CA-issued materials, and pg_stat_replication joined with pg_stat_ssl shows ssl=t for both standby connections both before and after the full restart cycle.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-116cc494e2414652\",\"cmd-9e12314833d94f93\",\"cmd-53bf498d8e3a4132\",\"cmd-d0d3c7d2ae0a4bef\",\"cmd-4bad63cc11e9439f\",\"cmd-ca1501fa4b0a4958\",\"cmd-11ab52ca33db4a58\",\"cmd-b04cead12b9b4cb3\",\"cmd-953f1bc5a56847d6\",\"cmd-d0632afd79f74a1e\",\"cmd-450b5156b79d4fb5\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3-cert-only-access\",\"requirement\":\"Accept replication connections only from peers presenting a certificate issued by that CA\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"pg_hba.conf on all three nodes uses 'hostssl replication replicator <peer-ip>/32 cert' restricted to the specific peer IPs, which requires TLS client-certificate authentication verified against the CA in ssl_ca_file. A directly observed negative test (no client cert supplied, PGSSLCERT/PGSSLKEY unset) was rejected with 'FATAL: connection requires a valid client certificate', and the positive path (replicator cert signed by the same CA) succeeded for both standbys' pg_basebackup and ongoing streaming. This demonstrates enforcement in both directions, though no test explicitly attempted a certificate signed by a different/foreign CA.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-06497b9f0705441f\",\"cmd-a9bb2535274c4e08\",\"cmd-f1717d4b54ad43a7\",\"cmd-7bca66830e0e4060\",\"cmd-4bad63cc11e9439f\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4-restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Independent provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: pre-restart boot identity/health, restart, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state for every managed node\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"All three nodes show pre-restart boot_id captured with healthy state, an explicit systemctl reboot issuance, polling through connection failures until reachable, a confirmed different post-restart boot_id, and recovered PostgreSQL/replication/TLS/data state per node. A final full-cluster check after all three restarts confirms both standbys still streaming over SSL and a newly inserted row replicated to both. Boot-identity values in the fixed after_prepare/after_executor global snapshots match the executor's own before/after values for each node, providing an independent cross-check.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2fe4c31c3d124a17\",\"cmd-78c278038f0b42b0\",\"cmd-b1b710c5c44b484d\",\"cmd-b04cead12b9b4cb3\",\"cmd-e0550197d45b42fd\",\"cmd-243942696a3d4350\",\"cmd-68ec40ad5d804311\",\"cmd-953f1bc5a56847d6\",\"cmd-0c229cbc2a35466b\",\"cmd-95c6fa242ba446c9\",